+# Design: The Belief Lab
+
+## Canvas and system
+
+- 1920 × 1080 canvas with a 120 px frame inset and a reserved lower footer.
+- Navy (`#0d2437`) and deep navy (`#0a1e2f`) establish the field.
+- Blue (`#3393d6`) structures information; gold (`#eaab2d`) signals a useful reframe or choice.
+- Proxima Nova, falling back to system sans-serif. Headings use 900 weight; supporting copy uses 400 or 700.
+
+## Composition
+
+A small track label and progress line remain stable across the lesson. Each beat has a short eyebrow, a large headline, and a single visual model. Text stays above 40 px except the declared chrome labels. Cards use white or subtle blue surfaces, 12 px corners, and generous spacing.
+
+## Beat visuals
+
+1. **Honest look:** the phrase “quiet beliefs” is framed like an item under examination.
+2. **Belief cards:** three quotes enter as separate cards; the word “protective” gives way to “keeps you smaller.”
+3. **Leverage:** skills, credibility, and relationships balance into more options.
+4. **Experiments:** three small paths replace one oversized leap.
+5. **Re-design:** four role blocks visibly shift into a better-fit arrangement.
+6. **One path:** a belief passes through a small experiment and becomes confidence; the final question remains on screen for reflection.
+
+## Motion
+
+All animation is deterministic and timeline-driven. Entrances last 0.4–0.6 seconds, with 0.14-second staggers. Scene content exits in 0.3 seconds while stable chrome remains. There are no infinite animations or autonomous timers.
